    "reason": "[ev-e6932b8a5ba9] states the subject and change: per-tunnel IPsec keys, set with a `+` sign in the secret, are mandatory in 1.16. It does not say what happens to an IPsec deployment whose secret lacks the `+` sign (e.g., agent failure, rejected key, fallback, traffic disruption). It also gives no secret format or setting that would identify exposed environments beyond \"uses IPsec\", and only points to the encryption_ipsec guide, which is not shown. The surrounding section adds nothing on this point; [ev-5d3c6d3080f0] covers removed IPsec Helm options, not the key format. The encryption_ipsec guide section on per-tunnel keys, or the linked PR, is needed to decide consequence and applicability.",
